# Calculator form fields (locked)

Every SectorCalc calculator (`*-pro.html`) MUST use the shared form layout so number digits never clip beside unit selectors.

## Canonical assets

- `public/sc-form-fields.css` — source of truth (also `@import`ed by `public/sc-theme.css`)
- Injected on every page by `scripts/inject-site-nav.mjs`
- Enforced by `scripts/verify-form-fields.mjs` (wired into `npm run build`)

## Required markup

**Lit / sidebar tools:**

```html
<div class="sc-input-wrap">
  <input class="sc-input" type="number" ...>
  <select class="sc-unit">...</select>
</div>
```

**Engine / panel tools (machining-style):**

```html
<div class="uwrap">
  <input type="number" ...>
  <select class="units">...</select>
</div>
```

## Forbidden

- `min-width: 0` on `.sc-input` or `.uwrap input` (allows digit clipping)
- Number + unit side-by-side without `.sc-input-wrap` / `.uwrap`
- Shipping a new `*-pro.html` without `sc-form-fields.css`
- Three narrow columns of numeric+unit fields without enough width (use max 2 cols)

## New tools

```bash
node scripts/new-tool.mjs --id SC-0XX --slug my-tool --title "My Tool" --kind lit
# or --kind engine
npm run build
```

Templates live in `content/templates/tool-pro-lit.html` and `tool-pro-engine.html`.
